{
  "abstract": "We study the rational sections associated with the fixed Diophantine anchors 1 and 3 on the degree-four extender cover. Writing q=u^2-3 and c=-4u(u-1)(u-3)/q^2, the compatible triple is represented by an elliptic K3 model over Q(u). We prove, with an injective specialization of the product twist, an independent 2-isogeny rank descent, exact fibre-height calculations and a sixteen-class two-Kummer computation, that its full section group is ZP direct sum ZR direct sum (Z/2)^2, with height matrix diag(2,1). Consequently every fourth entry in this field lies in one explicit coset (2m+1)P+j(2R). We then analyze two rational nodal fibres. Their section limits are nonnegative integers on a Pell conic. The exact integer extension theorem of Dujella and Petho forces the two members in each of the two nodal zero-loci to have indices summing to 0 or -1. Thus any septuple in this fixed section field extending the anchors has, up to negation and relabeling, four entries A_m,A_{-m-e},B_j,B_{-j-f}, with m,j positive and e,f binary. A formal-group calculation at the quadratic poles supplies an additional necessary squareclass condition for mixed-parity pairs. An independently replayed finite-field graph is included as calibration only. These are structural restrictions, not a construction or nonexistence theorem for rational septuples: further base changes and exceptional rational specializations remain outside the scope.",
